.TH EFFECTCRAFT-CLI 1 "November 2026" "EffectCraft 0.25.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
effectcraft\-cli \- EffectCraft from the command line: renderer, command runner and MCP server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B effectcraft\-cli
.I subcommand
.RI [ arguments ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B effectcraft\-cli
runs EffectCraft's editor commands without a window. It needs no windowing system and no GPU.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B info
Print a summary of the project and the engine.
.TP
.BR commands " [\-\-filter \fITEXT\fR] [\-\-enabled]"
List the engine commands.
.TP
.BI exec " command\-id " "" [ \-\-params " JSON" ]
Run one engine command.
.TP
.BR run " \fIid json\fR ..."
Run several commands in order. \fB\-\-args\-file\fR \fIF\fR and \fB\-\-commands\fR \fIFILE\fR|\fB\-\fR take the steps
from a file or from standard input.
.TP
.BI props " comp layer"
Print a layer's property tree with the paths of its properties.
.TP
.BI get " comp layer path"
Read a property.
.TP
.BI set " comp layer path value"
Set a property.
.TP
.B render\-frame
Render one frame of a composition, to PNG with
.BR \-\-out .
.TP
.B render
Render a composition to a file (\fB\-\-out\fR \fIFILE\fR), in the format given by
.B \-\-format
or guessed from the extension, or add it to the render queue with
.BR \-\-queue .
.TP
.BR script " \fIFILE.jsx\fR | \-\-eval \fICODE\fR"
Run JavaScript with the After Effects-style object model (\fBapp.project\fR, compositions, layers, properties).
.TP
.B mcp
Run an MCP server on standard input and output, so that an AI agent can drive the editor engine, headless or
attached to a running EffectCraft window.
.PP
.B replay
and
.B bench
are also subcommands; see the usage text.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print results as JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.PP
Running
.B effectcraft\-cli
without a valid subcommand prints the full usage, with all the options of the render subcommands.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR effectcraft (1)
.PP
https://getartcraft.com/apps/effectcraft
